{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP24 approved as refined on 2026-09-01. Correct the guide to document the complete bug workflow: bugs are exempt from plan review at claim time so agents can perform RCA before the remediation shape is known. For complex bugs, the LLM Review gate requires plan review after RCA, once the ticket contains an implementation plan and file impact, and before remediation implementation begins. The documentation must avoid both false extremes: plan review is not required before claiming every bug, and complex bug remediation is not exempt from later plan review."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788300005224864001,"uuid":"96bdd350-1ff0-4a81-a899-542326f1a2de"}